<title>HONG KONG: TENNIS-THAILAND TAKE 2-0 LEAD IN DAVIS CUP TIE.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-THAILAND TAKE 2-0 LEAD IN DAVIS CUP TIE.</headline>
<text>
<p>HONG KONG, Feb 14, Reuter - Thailand took a 2-0 lead over Hong Kong after the opening singles in their Davis Cup tennis Asia/Oceania Zone Group II first round tie on Friday.</p>
<p>Results (Thailand names first):</p>
<p>Vorapol Thongkhamchoo beat Mark Ferreira 6-3 6-2 6-0</p>
<p>Vittaya Samrej beat Melvin Tong 6-3 5-7 6-2 2-6 6-4.</p>
</text>
